CHAPTER.VERS:
If my step hath turned out of the way, and mine heart 

          That is, has accomplished the lust of my eyes.
         walked after mine eyes, and if any blot hath cleaved to mine hands;

If I did despise the cause of my manservant or of my maidservant, when they 

          When they thought themselves evil intreated by me.
         contended with me;

If I have withheld the poor from [their] desire, or have caused the eyes of the widow 

          By long waiting for her request.
         to fail;

If I beheld the 

          If I was proud of my worldly prosperity and happiness, which is meant by the shining of the sun, and brightness of the moon.
         sun when it shined, or the moon walking [in] brightness;

If my land 

          As though I had withheld their wages that laboured in it.
         cry against me, or that the furrows likewise thereof complain;
